+/*
+ * Qualcomm SDX55M in "Fusion" configuration: an SDX55 embedded in a phone with
+ * no flash of its own, so the host must supply the whole boot chain. Seen on the
+ * OnePlus 8T (kebab) and Xiaomi Mi 10T (apollo), both of which report PCI
+ * 17cb:0306 with subsystem 17cb:010c.
+ *
+ * BHI loads sbl1.mbn as usual, but AMSS does *not* arrive over BHIe/FBC: the SBL
+ * asks for images one at a time over the Sahara v2 protocol on MHI channels 2/3,
+ * which only exist in the SBL execution environment. Pushing AMSS over BHIe
+ * instead makes the SBL reject the vector with BHIE_TXVECSTATUS_STATUS_ERROR,
+ * which is what an earlier attempt on kebab hit. mhi_sahara_modem
+ * (CONFIG_MHI_BUS_SAHARA_MODEM) binds to the SAHARA channel and serves those
+ * requests; amss_fw reaches it via mhi_controller::amss_image.
+ *
+ * Firmware lives in /lib/firmware/sdx55m/ (no qcom/ prefix) because the Sahara
+ * loader builds its paths that way.
+ */
